      "confidence": 0.7,
      "curator_note": "MH+ of 7-ethoxybicyclo[3.2.0]heptan-2-one, protonated on the ketone (arrow label 'i'). Grob/retro-[2+2]-type ring opening of the cyclobutane: the C3-C4 bond (fusion carbon to ethoxy carbon) cleaves as the ring C1=C3 enol double bond forms and the ethoxy oxygen O5 lone pair closes the C4=O5+ oxocarbenium, relaying the charge from the ketone O2 to the ether O5. ARC COUNT (zoomed re-read): the book draws 2 arc(s): arc 1 = carbonyl pi (C1=O2) collapsing onto O2 (neutralising the protonated ketone to the enol OH) = move 1; arc 2 = the cyclobutane C3-C4 sigma bond forming the new ring C1=C3 double bond (arrowhead at the carbonyl carbon C1) = move 2. Move 3 (the ethoxy O5 lone pair forming C4=O5+ oxocarbenium) is an IMPLICIT hook required for electron balance -- it is NOT drawn on the page (the region around the ethoxy carbon C4 shows only a bold/hashed stereo wedge, no curved arrow). The H's on the fusion carbons are stereochemistry labels, not migrating: no atom changes its H count in this step. Scheme (b) is the trans/exo ring-fusion diastereomer of (a); with stereochemistry omitted it has identical connectivity and opens to the same intermediate, so it is not encoded as a separate record."
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev_step_retroene",
      "source_id": "mclafferty_ims_4e",
      "target_type": "step",
      "target_id": "step_retro_ene_elimination",
      "support_type": "textbook_proposed",
      "locator": {
        "page": 159,
        "equation": "8.30",
        "figure": null,
        "panel": null,
        "section": "8.3 Steric factors"
      },
      "confidence": 0.75,
      "curator_note": "Second 'i' step: the ring-opened oxocarbenium enol expels ethyl vinyl ether and reforms protonated cyclopent-2-enone (drawn 100%). A 4-arrow retro-ene/retro-Michael cascade: enol O2 lone pair -> C1=O2+ (reform protonated carbonyl); C1=C3 pi -> C3=C9 (new conjugated ring C=C); C9-C8 sigma -> C8=C4 (forms the vinyl ether C=C, cleaving C8-C9 to release the neutral); C4=O5+ pi -> O5 lone pair (neutralises the oxocarbenium to the ether oxygen). Book draws all 4 arcs in the central intermediate (arc at HO->C1, arc within the ring C=C toward C9, arc from the C9-C8 chain toward the oxocarbenium, and the small arc at =O5+-Et). No implicit hooks."
    },
